{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1481252-do-wraiths-show-up-on-camera-and-film","id":1481252,"title":"Do Wraiths show up on camera and film?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-16T12:35:36-07:00","id":1481252,"title":"Do Wraiths show up on camera and film?","content":"Do Wraiths show up on camera and film? If so, does it require a special type of camera or film? Does the Wraith have to be manifesting in some way or using a particular Arcanoi, or can their image be captured if they just happen to in view of the camera while on the other side of the Shroud?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T17:19:10-07:00","id":1481322,"title":"","content":"The general answer is &quot;no&quot; although a Wraith manifesting with Embody probably shows something (not necessarily a clear picture, but something), and I would say if they were able to Materialize they would show. If they weren't using Embody, then they probably don't appear at all.<br /> <br /> However, I am a great fan of trying to simulate real world folklore, paranormal, and occult stories in the game. And in the real world, many paranormal investigators insist that when they take photographs that the appearances of &quot;orbs&quot;, &quot;glows&quot;, and other strange lighting effects are proof of ghosts. So as an ST, I would be inclined to occasionally have photographs show that when Wraiths are present provided either the Shroud is low, it's in a Haunt, a Nihil is nearby, a Wraith is utilizing some Arcanos that is affecting the Skinlands, or some other strange thing that might &quot;bleed&quot; through the Shroud. (And I'd have it the effect be bad enough that most people think it's just bad photography that does not prove anything.) I don't think there are any rules to that effect though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}